  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;No additional punctuations in the external walls or roofs shall be permitted beyond those shown on the approved drawings.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON: To protect the architectural integrity and historic character of the listed building.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;No cleaning of masonry other than low-pressure (20–100 psi) nebulous water spray is authorised. Any alternative cleaning methods require written approval and a test panel.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON: To ensure appropriate conservation cleaning methods.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;All new works and making-good to the retained fabric shall match the original work in materials, method, dimensions, profile, colour, finish, facebond and pointing.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON: To maintain consistency with the historic fabric and appearance of the building.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;Where second-hand or salvaged bricks are used, they shall be fully cleaned of all coatings prior to reuse.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON: To ensure compatibility with the existing historic building.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "<p>The Development hereby permitted shall only be carried out and completed strictly in accordance with the submitted plans hereby approved and any subsequent approval of details.\r\n</p><p><br></p><p>\r\nREASON: To ensure that the development hereby permitted is carried out in full accordance with the plans hereby approved.\r\n</p>",
    "<p>The Development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of this consent.</p><p><br></p><p>\r\nREASON: In order to comply with the provisions of Section 18(a) of the Planning (Listed Buildings and Conservation Areas) Act 1990 as amended.\r\n</p>",
    "&lt;p&gt;Before work begins, proposals for the method and extent of repointing shall be approved in writing with the Local Planning Authority and be carried out accordingly. The required detail shall include 1 metre square sample panels showing the proposed joints, mortar mix, profile and finish. No other repointing of brickwork is authorised without prior approval.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON: To ensure appropriate conservation methods in accordance with national and local heritage policy.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;All historic fabric removed from the building shall be subject to a full photographic and textual recording to Historic England Level 3. The record shall be submitted to the LPA, the Greater London Historic Environment Record and Hackney Archives prior to occupation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON: To ensure significant historic fabric is properly recorded prior to removal.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;All existing historic features including, but not limited to, chimney pieces, plasterwork, architraves, panelling, and doors, shall remain undisturbed in their existing position and shall be fully protected during the course of works, unless specifically authorised otherwise.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON: To protect the special historic and architectural interest of the listed building.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;No soil stacks, soil vent pipes, plumbing, pipes, flues, vents, ductwork, grilles, alarms, lighting, or cameras shall be fixed on the external faces of the building other than those shown on the approved drawings.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON: To preserve the appearance of the listed building.&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
